      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I dealt with this for a couple of weeks off and on, specifically launching VRChat (and the very rare time during). I could usually get it to trigger semi-consistently if I was at a moderate to high CPU load while launching the game (also still happened with low or no load at all).\n\nEverything I could find online, and checking some of the dump files, pointed to it being an EAC issue. Though, like OP, this affected *only* VRChat and not any other EAC games.\n\nRan similar stress tests with my hardware, disabling any overclocks, etc. Nothing was wrong, and the issue persisted.\n\nWeirdly enough, my 'fix' was enabling Memory Integrity under Core isolation in Windows Security (despite it allegedly sometimes causing issues with EAC). I'd assume now Windows is blocking EAC from accessing somewhere in memory it shouldn't be. Since then, no more BSOD or anything outside of the normal crash here and there from large instances.\n\nThere may be other games out there that have this similar issue, but everything from my experience, points towards this being a VRC EAC issue specifically (maybe with newer builds of Windows?).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-08-04T22:42:48.195Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "1. Either happens immediately after launching VR chat or after taking my headset off for an extended period of time. Oddly enough, this only happens in VR chat no other game I own will do this.\n\n2. I've ruled out this being hardware related by running memtest 86 on my ram, updating my bios and corroborating it with someone else's findings on the VR chat forms which can be found here https://ask.vrchat.com/t/recurring-bsod-0x1a-memory-management/48768\n\n3. This has been happening to me for sometime guessing maybe two or three months now and I haven't been able to find a workaround for it. \n\nI'd appreciate it any attention this gets and if you need anything else from me, I'm here :)",
